    <section id="with-non-image-elements">
      <title>With non-image elements</title>
      <p>Place additional DITA elements within a <xmlelement
        >grid-row</xmlelement> element to add them within a carousel.
        Additional structure and spacing can be added by using the <xmlelement>grid-col</xmlelement> element.</p>
    </section>
    <example>
      <ol outputclass="carousel">
        <li>
          <div outputclass="row">
            <div outputclass="col-1"/>
            <div outputclass="col-10">
              <lines outputclass="p-1 theme-secondary theme-muted theme-border">Is it for fear to wet a widow’s eye
That thou consum’st thyself in single life?
Ah, if thou issueless shalt hap to die,
The world will wail thee like a makeless wife;</lines>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div outputclass="row">
            <div outputclass="col-1"/>
            <div outputclass="col-10">
              <lines
                outputclass="p-1 theme-secondary theme-muted theme-border"
              >The world will be thy widow and still weep
That thou no form of thee hast left behind,
When every private widow well may keep,
By children’s eyes, her husband’s shape in mind.</lines>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div outputclass="row">
            <div outputclass="col-1"/>
            <div outputclass="col-10">
              <lines
                outputclass="p-1 theme-secondary theme-muted theme-border"
              >Look what an unthrift in the world doth spend
Shifts but his place, for still the world enjoys it;
But beauty’s waste hath in the world an end,
And, kept unused, the user so destroys it.</lines>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div outputclass="row">
            <div outputclass="col-1"/>
            <div outputclass="col-10">
              <lines
                outputclass="p-1 theme-secondary theme-muted theme-border"
              > No love toward others in that bosom sits
 That on himself such murd’rous shame commits.

            <b>Sonnet 9 - William Shakespeare</b></lines>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </example>
